    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: The project is currently in progress, aiming to achieve its objectives upon the completion of ongoing works.

Water Supply: So far 1,591 km of water supply pipes have been installed, exceeding the targeted 1,350 km. Furthermore, 80,447 household connections have been established.

Sanitation: So far 1,151 km of sewer pipes have been laid out of the targeted 1,300 km.

Institutional and human capacities strengthened: Orientation sessions have been conducted for ward councilors, ULB staff, and line departments, engaging a total of 750 participants. MOU has been executed with 14 Government Engineering Colleges and 13 Private Engineering Colleges for a women&apos;s internship program, with two batches already completed, totaling 56 participants.

Overall, the project has achieved approximately 75% physical progress, and it is anticipated that the desired outcomes will be attained by the targeted year 2028.</narrative>
